---
description: Python and ML conventions for Bible AI Assistant
globs: ["**/*.py", "**/*.ipynb"]
alwaysApply: true
---

- Use Python 3.13+ syntax with type hints on all functions
- Use f-strings, never .format() or % formatting
- Use pathlib, never os.path for file operations
- Use conda environment: bible-ai-assistant for this project
- GPU: RTX 5070 Ti, 16GB VRAM, Blackwell sm_120, PyTorch 2.10+cu128
- Use torch.cuda.amp.autocast() for any inference or training
- Bible corpus in world-english-bible/ is READ-ONLY — never write to it
- All LLM calls tested locally via Ollama before any external API usage
- Use parameterized queries for any database operations — never string concat
- Log retrieval quality metrics when modifying RAG pipeline
- Structure: src/, data/, notebooks/, tests/, models/
- NEVER commit .env files or API keys
- Use descriptive variable names (verse_embeddings not ve)
